# NO BLANKET *.mjs RULE HERE. There used to be `/*.mjs`, meant to keep the scratch
# harnesses I write at the repo root out of history. It also swallowed
# postcss.config.mjs, which meant Vercel cloned a repo with no PostCSS config, ran its
# default minify-only pipeline, and never loaded the Tailwind plugin. The deployed CSS
# shipped with `@tailwind base;` and `@apply ...` as literal text -- invalid CSS the
# browser silently drops -- so every utility class on the site had nothing behind it
# while the hand-written rules kept working. It looked like a broken stylesheet, or a
# CDN problem, or deployment protection. It was one line in this file.
#
# Ignore scratch scripts by name if they turn up. Never by extension.
